/Contents (Primordial Big Bang nucleosynthesis proposes the formation of nuclides ^2H, ^3He ^4He and ^7Li for roughly half an hour following the universe's 3rd minute of existence. It agrees well with observational data for all of these except ^7Li, for which it overestimates the abundances by a factor of three. This is the 'cosmological lithium problem'.)
